WEBVTT

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.450
Okay, go right.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.250
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffy, fluffy, fluffy...

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.830
Now, left.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:19.830
Yffulf, yffulf, yffulf, yffulf, yffulf...

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.790
Okay, now back to the right. Ready? Go!

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.790
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffy, fluffy, fluffy...

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.700
Then, left.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:36.500
Scarfs are warm, but they feel
so prickly on my neck.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.160
Next time we do these fluffy exercises,

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.370
let's not do them with the scarves.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:51.410
Hey, what's this stuff coming from your hair?

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.370
Um... I'm not quite sure, either.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:00.370
Huh...? Then I shall solve this mystery for you.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.870
Do you think you're up to the task, Little?

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:08.660
Don't test me! I got a hundred
on my science test before!

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.700
Oho... Then I shall give you this.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:20.410
Ow... Now, Little. Give me your hand.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.660
Come, come.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:22.660
Okay.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.950
You go like this...

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.040
And then, like this...

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.790
You must solve the mystery
in order to free your finger!

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:38.160
Seriously?

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:50.000
W-Well, I'm gonna solve this in a jiffy
and get rid of this thing!

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.330
Just you wait, Yachi.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.830
By the way, who is this Yachi you speak of?

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.080
Welcoming the New Year by studying...

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.410
When did I become such an honor student?

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:15.870
"Are you awake?"

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.580
"Are you awake?"

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.580
Adachi?

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.580
Uh... Yeah, I'm awake.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:25.580
Wow, that was fast.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.950
"Can I call you?"

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.450
Hello? Sure, you can call me.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.910
It's rare for you to call me.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.580
Look who's talking.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.790
So, was this some kind of emergency?

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.500
Not really. I just...

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.000
...wanted to give you a call.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.330
Huh...?

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:18.870
Were you watching TV?

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.790
Um...

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.870
Maybe.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.830
Wait, what kind of answer is that?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.370
By the way, did you know?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.660
This year's almost done.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.000
Yeah.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.790
Are you doing anything for New Year's?

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:39.290
We basically just go to my grandparents' place
for a bit, but that's it.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.910
Do you get New Year's money?

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:46.200
Oh, yeah. I guess I do...

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.330
Shimamura? Shimamura?

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:58.330
Oh, sorry. I was just remembering your thighs.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.250
Huh?! M-My thighs...

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.700
Yeah, they're pretty nice.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:14.160
O-Oh, really? I-I see...

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.000
What's wrong?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.410
What's wrong? Well, you just...

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.950
Huh? Me?

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.750
Was that sexual harassment?

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:30.290
Huh? That wasn't sexual harassment.
That was a totally normal thing to say.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.120
Why my thighs?

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:35.790
I was just thinking how nice
your lap pillow was.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.620
Oh, because I'm lying down right now.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.330
I see.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.080
Ayup.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:50.620
Would you prefer me
to make them harder or softer?

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.540
What?

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:55.750
My thighs. Which would you prefer?

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.700
I think they're fine just the way they are.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.950
I'll do my best not to gain weight!

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:06.120
You should probably worry about
not losing too much weight.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.000
Oh, yeah. I'm drinking that tea. Thank you.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.000
I'm also, uh...

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.410
...using that thing all the time.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.080
It's the New Year.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.660
Should we do New Year greetings?

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.370
Yeah.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.450
Happy New Year.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.580
Happy New Year.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.750
Let's keep hanging out this year.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.120
Yeah.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.080
Okay, I'm going to bed.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.660
Okay. Goodnight.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.200
Goodnight.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.540
"Goodnight" sounds nice...

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.500
Hm? Sounds nice?

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:55.120
Oh, it's nothing!

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:03.450
Did she just want to wish me a Happy New Year?

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.580
But I want to be like, your best friend.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:12.830
That shouldn't be too hard. I mean,
I don't have that many friends.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:16.410
I sorta really want to be that, so...

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.620
Even if I told her she already was,

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.830
I didn't think it'd make her happy.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:30.870
Because even if the phrase "best friend"
may sound the same when we say it,

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:34.830
there might be a difference in our
actual definition of the phrase.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.200
The level that Adachi wants
to take this relationship

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:43.750
was so impossibly high that I'd probably
need to sprout wings to even attain it.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:58.830
I need to work harder this year.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.620
I say that and then immediately do this.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:09.580
I think how I feel about Shimamura's chest
will basically determine things.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:13.660
What exactly I want from Shimamura

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.870
should be determined there.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.790
I...

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:31.750
Do I want to see Shimamura's chest?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:40.040
I guess... I can't say I don't want to see them.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.410
But I wouldn't say I'd particularly
pursue this venture, either.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.750
O-Oh, so it's pretty normal.

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:04.040
My feelings for Shimamura are pure,

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.620
and I like Shimamura as a person.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.080
Goodnight, Adachi.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.910
Gosh, I love "Goodnight."

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:22.620
There shouldn't be an issue if I dove
into Shimamura's bosom right now.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.910
Because I'm completely normal...

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.200
Her face? Her chest?

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:42.040
Uh, wait... That's not...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:09.000
Wait, what? What's going on?

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:14.080
Is this what they mean by the biter gets bit?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.290
Actually, I think "digging my own grave"
is more fitting.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:21.620
I can't separate my struggles
from Shimamura just yet.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.040
Just when I was thinking

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:29.580
that my dye job was beginning to fade,

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.830
"2/4 (Tues)"

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.830
it's now February.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.950
Winter break had ended,
we got new seating assignments,

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.450
and I was finally getting used to
said seating assignment.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.830
January was over in a blink of an eye,
and now it's February.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.660
As usual, Adachi seems to be acting weird.

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.370
I mean, Adachi's always acting weird, but...

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.580
When our eyes meet, she looks away.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:58.620
I try to ask if she wants to hang out
and she ends up running away.

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:03.410
I'm pretty sure that these past few days,
I haven't even heard her voice.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:06.410
Why does she have to be such a troublemaker?

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:12.830
Hey, hey, hey. Hey, yo, Shima! I'm Hino!

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:14.120
How are you?

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:19.250
This isn't Hawaii and winter break
ended a month ago.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:23.120
I didn't actually need anything. Bye!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.620
Is she throwing that thing around?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.870
Huh?

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.370
What else would I be talking about?
You know, the boomerang.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:35.540
Oh... Yeah, I'm sure, uh,
my little sister is throwing it around.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.410
Tell her I challenge her to a duel
once she gets better.

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:40.370
Uh, sure.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.410
Uh, Shimamura!

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.120
Hey.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.040
H-Hey.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.580
Um, uh...

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.450
Are you free today?

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.080
Hm?

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:03.200
Let's go somewhere far away... Wait, no.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.910
I was wondering if you wanted to
stop by someplace after school...

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.870
...or something.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.870
Did you want to go somewhere?

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.660
I mean, we don't have to if you're busy.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.290
It's up to you.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:21.950
I see. Well, that's a relief.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:25.540
Because I'm so insanely busy today...

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.660
Huh? Of course, I'm not busy.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:33.370
You don't have to rub that in, Adachi.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.370
Sorry.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.580
I was lying when I said I was busy.
So let's go somewhere. Sorry.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.580
Huh? Uh...

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.830
So, did you have somewhere in mind?

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:54.000
N-Not anywhere exact, but...

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.040
"But"...?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:59.500
U-Um... I think I want some snacks.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:03.080
So Miss Adachi would like some sweets?

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:06.660
Um, yup... Snacks.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.120
Would you prefer something not sweet?

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:12.500
Yeah, er... Something sweet is fine.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.580
So, where should we go?

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.290
Y-Yeah...

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:30.410
Adachi?

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.410
Can I?

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:34.620
Can you what?

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:40.290
Oh, my hand. Here. Go ahead.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.450
So, we're going to have something sweet, right?

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.750
Y-Yeah.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.500
There's a donut shop right here.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.330
They don't have it...

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:07.200
Maybe not there.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.870
Really?

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.250
Would you prefer Japanese sweets, then?

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:15.290
That's not what I meant. I think...

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.410
Did you have somewhere in mind?

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:21.290
Oh, uh... No, I don't.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:27.830
Oh, yeah. I wanted to ask you.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:32.750
Should I dye my hair again or go back to black?

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.830
Hm... Hmm...

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:44.370
I'm not sure because I've never
seen you with black hair.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:49.450
Well, I am the purest little
Snow White you'll find.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:57.000
Look. My hair's starting to grow out,
so I was wondering what I should do.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.120
Is something wrong?

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:08.200
I-It's nothing.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:15.410
What about here? We can get takeout
and eat on the bench.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.450
Adachi?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.080
Yeah, uh, that's great.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.160
Huh?

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:30.950
"Heart <i>Chocolat</i>"

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.500
"Valentine's Day Fair"

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:39.370
Do you mind if I try lifting?

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.160
Lifting what?

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.540
You.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.080
Why, though?

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.000
Because I think I can.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:51.040
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.620
Hup!

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:03.290
I'm floating! I'm floating! Wait... Ow, ow.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.830
Hey, my armpits hurt! Hey!

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.330
Oh, sorry.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.540
You were heavier than I thought.

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:17.370
Jeez, how rude can you be?

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.040
So, what exactly were you trying to do?

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.910
Nothing. I just figured I could lift you up.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.910
Oh, never mind.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:30.040
By the way, did you want chocolate this year?

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.450
I love sweet things.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:35.330
Alrighty. I guess I'll buy you
something again this year.

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:38.330
"Valentine's Day Fair"

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.410
Valentine's... It says Valentine's.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:43.330
It sure does.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:48.080
I... guess it's that time of year...

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.910
Yup.

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.120
What about Valentine's?

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.660
Uh, I, uh...

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:58.910
It's not... a big deal...

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.200
Oh, me?

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.160
Whoa.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:35.370
U-Um, I was just...

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.540
Um, I...

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:47.120
Did Adachi bring me here just to
show me this Valentine's poster?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.830
That was so much trouble.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:52.250
Or I guess I should just say that was
a rather roundabout way of doing this.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:00.750
Do you have any plans on the 14th, Shimamura?

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.080
I do not.

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:07.000
I-If you don't, could we hang out
on the 14th, maybe?

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:14.790
Um... Do you want chocolate or do you
want to give me chocolate?

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:15.910
Huh?!

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:20.870
I, uh... Um...

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:21.870
Gimme.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:27.450
N-No, I mean, either. Or rather, let's exchange!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.580
Ah, friendship chocolate.

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:36.500
I'm pretty sure Hino and Nagafuji
do something like that every year.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:39.790
But I don't see this going
as smoothly as it'd go for them.

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.160
They've been doing this for years.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:47.290
But isn't the point to give someone chocolate
suddenly that day as a surprise?

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:52.410
I wonder how many years I'll be around Adachi.

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:54.500
Maybe just until graduation?

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.790
Actually, once we move up a year,
we might end up in different classes

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:00.290
and that might be the end of it.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.910
I...

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.700
I prefer knowing.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:09.500
Because there's actually some hope
knowing it might happen.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.120
Is that how it is?

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:20.250
There're still plenty of problems.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:25.700
Adachi was trying to take a step out
of the flow of our day-to-day life.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:27.080
I can't help but think

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:31.370
that whatever direction she's taking,
it's always facing me.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:37.120
And I can't help but admire
her determination and resolve.

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:38.950
And that's why...

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:47.830
Sure. Let's do Valentine's Day this year.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:20:01.120
For me, every day just seemed grey and endless.

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:04.330
But on this day, February 4th,

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:07.000
and the next ten days of grey,

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:11.700
seemed to slowly have color added to them.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.790
Shimamura!

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:57.040
I want to die.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:35.750
Hey, working hard?

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:39.950
Hey. Getting side dishes for dinner?

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:40.950
Yup.

00:22:40.950 --> 00:22:43.160
Let's see, today, I'll get...

00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:44.620
Shima?

00:22:56.580 --> 00:22:57.660
Tarumi?

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:00.950
Yeah, it's me! It's been forever.

00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:04.160
You sorta became really pretty.

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:06.540
Was "sorta" necessary?

00:23:06.540 --> 00:23:08.080
Here you go.

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:09.910
Thank you.

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:10.870
See you later.

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:12.620
Yeah, sure.

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.750
Later, huh...?

00:23:19.950 --> 00:23:22.080
Can I get your number?

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:24.540
Oh. Yeah, sure.

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:30.000
Nagafuji had witnessed something.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.040
Much lower key than a housewife
witnessing something, but...

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:34.580
Thanks.

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:40.080
I'll give you a call when I get home.

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:41.450
Sure.

00:23:42.410 --> 00:23:44.080
So, yeah...

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:45.370
Later.

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:54.540
"Episode 7: 'Please Choose
the Best Chocolate for Me'"

00:23:54.540 --> 00:23:58.040
"Episode 7: 'Please Choose
the Best Chocolate for Me'"
"Tarumi"

